            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<h4><strong>When the Filter Needs a Refresh</strong> </h4><p></p><p>Over time, Blueair filters fill up with everything they’ve captured — dust, smoke, particles, and odors — and that’s when they need a well-earned retirement. </p><p>Most filters last around six to nine months, depending on how often you run your purifier (and how spooky your environment gets). When it’s time, your Blueair app or device light will give you a gentle nudge. </p><p>Changing a filter is as easy - pop the old one out, slide the new one in, and reset the indicator. Voilà — your air is refreshed, and your purifier is ready for another season of keeping the monsters (and allergens) at bay. </p><p> </p><h4><strong>The Freshest Kind of Fright</strong> </h4><p></p><p>This Halloween, let your house be spooky for the right reasons. Keep your skeletons in the closet (and the dust bunnies out of the air). Between Blueair’s powerful HEPASilent™ purification and their lineup of filters — from <strong>Particle</strong> to <strong>SmokeBlock</strong> — you’ll have all the tools you need to keep your air fresh, your lungs happy, and your haunted vibe perfectly chill. </p><p>Because there’s nothing scarier than bad air — and nothing sweeter than breathing easy after a night of fright. </p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        }
